# Two generated artifacts are compared byte for byte against what their
# generator emits: `app/ui/src/bindings/vcw.d.ts` by
# `crates/contract/tests/bindings.rs` and `docs/SCHEMA.md` by
# `crates/project/tests/schema_doc.rs`. Both generators emit LF, and the
# index holds LF, so a checkout that converts to CRLF makes the comparison
# fail on a tree nobody has touched. That is what `test (windows-x86_64)`
# did on run 37413694623 while every other platform passed.
#
# Repository-wide rather than two patterns, because the next byte-compared
# file would have the same problem and would be found the same slow way.
# `text=auto` leaves anything git detects as binary alone, which is every
# .webp, .png and .aup3 in here.
* text=auto eol=lf
